{"id": "EUVD-2026-76263", "enisaUuid": "f0f18532-a903-3e8b-b210-87a40d1f67d2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: rtw88: pci: fix resource leak on failed NAPI setup\n\nrtw_pci_probe() allocates PCI resources through\nrtw_pci_setup_resource() before it sets up NAPI. If\nrtw_pci_napi_init() fails, the error path jumps straight to\nerr_pci_declaim and skips rtw_pci_destroy(), leaving the PCI\nresources allocated by rtw_pci_setup_resource() behind.\n\nAdd a dedicated cleanup label for the NAPI setup failure path so probe\ndestroys the PCI resources.\n\nThe bug was first flagged by an experimental analysis tool we are\ndeveloping for kernel memory-management bugs while analyzing current\nmainline kernels. The tool is still under development and is not yet\npublicly available. Manual inspection confirms that the bug is still\npresent in v7.1-rc7.\n\nAn x86_64 allyesconfig build showed no new warnings. As we do not have a\nsuitable rtw88 PCI board to test with, no runtime testing was able to be\nperformed.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:24", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/481fff9bda01720c70b19fb260808145a3f21594", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/34a505071d1ffc5ebf3dc3cd16d2a12b044bcc84", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b1596e212ab1739930b25b9d3daf6b5cd307b537", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e779df4806cd29cbcca5c9dc0a1073662c76b889"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80940", "GHSA-82xc-pjrp-m39r"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f3a1f7c-6cbb-39dc-aeec-2b304abad83d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "13bab379-b385-38b4-a010-5512182b7209", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "1460b916-defd-3951-96c2-9b942538393a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "27ec48db-5476-3fff-8f58-25aaf1a0cc98", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d0bcb10e7b94861c714ab1e62c98bf8abaa37527 <481fff9bda01720c70b19fb260808145a3f21594"}, {"id": "56ba0bdc-d73f-3a0e-8ebd-5e5b518dc035", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d0bcb10e7b94861c714ab1e62c98bf8abaa37527 <e779df4806cd29cbcca5c9dc0a1073662c76b889"}, {"id": "8e3899db-e4c8-368c-9adc-453343e9667c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d0bcb10e7b94861c714ab1e62c98bf8abaa37527 <34a505071d1ffc5ebf3dc3cd16d2a12b044bcc84"}, {"id": "8ec74415-cef5-3c6c-84c3-3883119e777f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "9a77f49b-e3ea-3dc7-93ab-4ad7e7608666", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "9c1ba0d5-53bb-317f-8b50-775a20c21c79", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d0bcb10e7b94861c714ab1e62c98bf8abaa37527 <b1596e212ab1739930b25b9d3daf6b5cd307b537"}, {"id": "b7eb3e34-7d3b-353f-ab22-6df4977dca19", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3d4f401a-b12d-375e-8c9e-15ea43713e91", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}